# Codex: Guide for Translating to Spanish

> **Prefix:** `codex-` | **Type:** Reference Manual | **Scope:** Translation to Spanish (es)

## Conventions

- Impersonal voice: "Se debe configurar..." not "Debes configurar..."
- Always use opening ¿ and ¡ marks
- Neutral Spanish, no regionalisms

## False Cognates (pt-BR ↔ es)

esquisito≠exquisito, polvo≠polvo, largo≠largo, escritório≠escritorio, sobrenome≠sobrenombre.

## False Cognates (en ↔ es)

actual≠actual (use "current"), sensible≠sensible (use "sensitive"), eventually≠eventualmente (use "finally").

## Formalization

- Obligation: "Se **DEBE** configurar..." (not "Tienes que")
- Necessity: "Es necesario..." (not "Hace falta")
- Recommendation: "Se recomienda..." (not "Estaría bien que")
